## Objective
- Fulfill GitHub issue `promikailamin/ultron_smp#12`: "In twingate admin panel there is no resources has been created fix it" by making a Twingate Resource named `minecraft` exist/be created automatically.

## Important Details
- Repo is actually a Minecraft/Fabric server repo despite the "chess image processing" project description.
- Twingate connector tokens (`TWINGATE_ACCESS_TOKEN`, `TWINGATE_REFRESH_TOKEN`) cannot create Resources; Resource automation requires an Admin API token (`TWINGATE_API_TOKEN`, Settings > API, Read & Write). Current repo secrets do NOT include `TWINGATE_API_TOKEN`, only connector tokens plus `TWINGATE_NETWORK`.
- Twingate Admin API: `POST https://<network>.twingate.com/api/graphql/`, header `X-API-KEY`.
- Tenant endpoints redirect with HTTP 308 to a regional host, e.g. `https://<network>.us2.twingate.com/api/graphql/`; Python `urllib` does not auto-follow 308.
- Forcing `socket.getaddrinfo` to `AF_INET` caused `socket.gaierror: [Errno -3] Temporary failure in name resolution`; that patch has been removed.
- Resource defaults: name `minecraft`, address `127.0.0.1`, TCP port `25565` restricted, UDP/ICMP disabled.
- Remote network selection: use the only network if one; otherwise `TWINGATE_REMOTE_NETWORK` (name) or `TWINGATE_REMOTE_NETWORK_ID`.
- System rules: commit/push incrementally to `main`, use `PAT_TOKEN`, never leak tokens, comment on issue #12 with `gh issue comment "12" --repo "promikailamin/ultron_smp" --body "..."` when done, do not claim tests passed/pushed unless true.
- Git identity is not configured on the runner; use `git config user.name "ultron"` and `git config user.email "ultron@users.noreply.github.com"`.
- Runner workspace: `/home/runner/work/ultron_smp/ultron_smp`.

